# Overview
#
# `in order to` says in three words what `to` says in one (`Run make in
# order to build it`). The two extra words tell the reader nothing. The
# fix writes `to` (`Run make to build it`), and the rule offers that
# rewrite. The rule sits at Required, because it matches one exact
# phrase and the fix is mechanical.
#
# Related Rules
#
# ProseWordy reports other phrases that have a one-word form and leaves
# out `in order to`, so only this rule reports the phrase.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 88 lines in the measure.py corpus, and in 20 of 20
# sampled hits `to` said the same.
expr main in order to
let message "`in order to`. Write `to`."
let description "Shortens `in order to`."
let becomes "to"
let kind "Style"
test "Run make in order to build it." "Run make to build it."
allows "Run make to build it."
